<% page_title "License" %>
<% page_description "What an AI Pop Music subscription lets you do with a downloaded track." %>

<article class="wrap measure">
  <h1 class="text-4xl">License</h1>

  <p class="meta mt-3">Version <%= Rails.application.config.x.license_terms_version %></p>

  <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-ink-600">
    This page is the licence. Every download records its version, so you can always show
    which terms applied to the file you hold.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-600">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">What you may do</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">With an active subscription, and a track from a genre your plan covers, you may:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
        <li>Use the track in unlimited productions, including commercial work.</li>
        <li>Monetise those productions on any platform, including advertising revenue.</li>
        <li>Edit, shorten, loop, pitch, and mix the track into your work.</li>
        <li>Use it for clients, as part of paid work you deliver to them.</li>
        <li>Keep using productions you made while subscribed, after the subscription ends.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">What you may not do</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
        <li>Redistribute or resell the track itself as a standalone music file, or as part of a
          music library, stock audio service, or dataset.</li>
        <li>Register the track, or a derivative, as a trademark or with a content-identification
          system as your own composition.</li>
        <li>Claim authorship of the underlying composition.</li>
        <li>Share your account or served download links with anyone else.</li>
        <li>Use the catalogue to train a machine-learning model.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Ownership and provenance</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Tracks in this catalogue are generated by us with YuE2 and are original output: they are
        not samples, covers, or re-recordings of existing recordings. We grant you the rights
        above; we do not transfer authorship of the composition.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Attribution</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Not required. Crediting "AI Pop Music" is welcome, never a condition.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Ending a subscription</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Downloads stop immediately, and future downloads from those genres are no longer
        available. Work you already published, or files you already downloaded while subscribed,
        remain licensed under the version in force when you downloaded them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Content identification</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        If a platform flags your production, send us the order number or the download record
        and we will confirm the licence. Keep your account email reachable: the download
        history is what makes that possible.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
